      },
      "message": "test(post): pin the G76 readings that two published manuals settle\n\nThree of the four open G76 readings of the Fanuc lathe post agree with\nthe FANUC 0i-F lathe operator's manual (B-64604EN-1, 4.2.7) and the\nSiemens SINUMERIK ISO Turning manual (A5E52211627B, G76): the start\npoint and the flank shift along the travel, every pass ending at the\nprogrammed end point, and the minimum depth clamping the cut of one\npass. New tests pin each one; the shared fixture moves to\ntests/common/g76.rs (the schedule suite stood at the 400-line law).\nThe internal rounding of dd*sqrt(n) stays open. No posted G-code\nchanges. Follow-up for the pass-end difference: #1896.\n\nRefs #1842\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
